ely has its downsides  especially for a toy who exists to bring  joy to children without a kid what's  Bo's purpose Bo Peep introduces her  story by saying that life on a baby lamp  isn't so exciting but she quickly back  tracks and says that sometimes it's  actually too exciting in the trailer she  is set on fire frozen and snow fights  stray cats and survives what looks like  a pretty crazy college party how did she  get into all of these crazy situations  it's safe to say that Bo Peep has been a  lot of places between Toy Story 2 and 4  we even get another glimpse at those  creepy Benson dolls that were the most  disturbing part of Toy Story 4 between  escaping dolls breaking one of her  porcelain arms and going through a  complete wardrobe change both seen and  done a lot of things before she finally  reunites with woody she struggled with  loneliness not being wanted by a new  child and adapting to a life as a  runaway where sure she has a lot to  share with woody about these crazy times  but the most important question is after  all the changes in growth she's  experienced is Bo Peep happy with how  things turned out Bo Peep story will be  told as a narration from Bo de woody as  they hang out on a carnival  rollercoaster so we can expect some very  personal stories about her fun and  emotional experiences as an unwanted toy  what we know about those life so far is  that when she was accidentally given  away she spent a couple of years sitting  on a shelf in an antique store and then  she spent some time as a toy to a kid  who didn't really want her this all  sounds pretty tragic for Bo but the  Shepherd is proved in Toy Story 4 that  she can roll with the punches with her  flock and woody by her side we're going  to find out everything Bo has learned  about herself during her daring  adventures as a renegade we know that  Tom Hanks will return as the voice of  woody along with Annie Potts is the  voice of Little Bo Peep we can probably  expect some other fun 